1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,325
The pressure built when the government changed the funding rule for the water utility.

2
00:00:04,325 --> 00:00:11,613
“The state will not carry the maintenance of a plant that the market cannot finance,” the minister said.

3
00:00:11,613 --> 00:00:21,876
“A dollar of public money has to buy a right, not a habit.” The declaration was short and the objection was long.

4
00:00:21,876 --> 00:00:26,235
The social argument was harder than the economic one.

5
00:00:26,235 --> 00:00:34,604
“A policy that works in the capital does not work in a community of four thousand,” a sociologist said.

6
00:00:34,604 --> 00:00:46,221
“The wealth of a society is not the same as the wealth of a sector.” The left wing of the council and the liberal bloc both claimed the phrase as their own.

7
00:00:46,221 --> 00:00:50,155
The civil question was who counted as a citizen.

8
00:00:50,155 --> 00:00:56,489
“A tax on water is not the same as a fee,” a socialist economist wrote.

9
00:00:56,489 --> 00:01:08,812
“One is a bill, the other is a bail for a utility that has already failed once.” The legal opinion on the table said the two could not be separated.

10
00:01:08,812 --> 00:01:13,801
The popular politics of the moment made the economics harder.

11
00:01:13,801 --> 00:01:33,122
“The market is not a democracy,” the mayor said, “and the interest of the taxpayer is not the interest of the citizen.” A dozen rates, four audits, and one red line across the page: the argument had a real shape at last.

12
00:01:33,122 --> 00:01:40,275
The pressure from the banks was simple: a declaration of socialism would close the credit line.

13
00:01:40,275 --> 00:01:46,534
“A dollar of funding deferred is a dollar of maintenance lost,” the treasurer said.

14
00:01:46,534 --> 00:01:54,988
The republican member disagreed, and so did the socialist member, and both of them were right.

15
00:01:54,988 --> 00:02:02,066
The act of the council was to hold the rate, off the record and on the condition of a second audit.

16
00:02:02,066 --> 00:02:06,960
“We can talk about capitalism later,” the mayor said.

17
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:16,593
“The pipe under this street will not wait.” The pressure had produced a decision, and the decision had produced the next pressure.

18
00:02:16,593 --> 00:02:25,431
The act of the council, the order of the day, and the real support of the four wards: all of it was on the record.

19
00:02:25,431 --> 00:02:38,348
Free water for the poor, a red line for the rich, and a republican objection from the left: the talk had a shape at last, and the issue was no longer off the table.

20
00:02:38,348 --> 00:02:53,410
The law was federal, the economy was local, and the citation of Marxism in a footnote about imperialism was, as one member said, a remark about civilisation rather than about the water bill.

21
00:02:53,410 --> 00:03:01,813
The only action left to the council was to wait, and the low point of the debate was still ahead.
